PAGE 3 — Categories, Attributes & Inventory Classification
Purpose
Provide a flexible hierarchy for grouping and controlling enterprise inventory.
The matrix explicitly requires inventory item categorization and configurable product attributes.
Example Hierarchy
Food & Beverage
→ Food
→ Meat
→ Beef
or:
Retail
→ Merchandise
→ Apparel
→ T-Shirts
or:
Operations
→ Maintenance
→ Electrical
→ Spare Parts
Classification Levels
TICVAI should support configurable structures such as:
 Division
 Department
 Category
 Subcategory
 Item Group
 Family
 Brand
 Commodity
 Usage Type
Category Defaults
A category may provide default settings for:
 UOM
 Tracking Method
 Shelf-Life Requirement
 Reorder Profile
 Approval Rules
 Accounting Mapping
 Warehouse Eligibility
 Storage Conditions
Dynamic Attributes
Example:
F&B Ingredient
 Temperature Class

