PAGE 7 — Inventory Status & Stock Control Rules
Purpose
Provide centralized configuration for how inventory may move between operational states.
The matrix requires tracking of available, reserved, on-order, in-transit and damaged inventory.
Standard Stock Statuses
I recommend supporting at minimum:
 Available
 Reserved
 Allocated
 Picked
 Packed
 In Transit
 On Order
 Inspection
 Quarantine
 Blocked
 Damaged
 Returned
 Expired
 Written Off

TICVAI / INVENTORY & PROCUREMENT BACKEND STRUCTURE
CONFIDENTIAL | 14
Status Transition Rules
Example:
Available
→ Reserved
→ Allocated
→ Picked
→ Dispatched
→ In Transit
→ Received
→ Available
Controlled Transitions
Examples:
Damaged
cannot become
Available
without inspection/approval.
Quarantine
cannot be sold or consumed.
Expired
cannot be released for normal use.
Module Rules
Stock status behavior may differ by operational context.
Example:
Retail Returned Item
→ Inspection
→ Available / Damaged
F&B Returned Ingredient
→ normally not returned to available consumption unless specifically approved.
Negative Inventory
The tenant shall determine:
 Negative Stock Not Allowed
 Warning Only
 Authorized Override
 Emergency Offline Exception
All overrides shall be audited.
