ITEM MASTER GOVERNANCE
The Inventory Item Master should support governance throughout its lifecycle.
Lifecycle
Draft
→ Review
→ Approved
→ Active
→ Suspended
→ Obsolete
→ Archived
Validation Before Activation
TICVAI should check:
✓ Unique Item Code
✓ Category
✓ Base UOM
✓ Inventory Behavior
✓ Tracking Method
✓ Accounting Mapping where required
✓ Barcode where required
✓ Storage Profile where required
Versioning
Significant master-data changes shall retain:
 Previous Value
 New Value
 Changed By
 Approved By
 Effective Date
 Reason

TICVAI / INVENTORY & PROCUREMENT BACKEND STRUCTURE
CONFIDENTIAL | 20
BARCODE / QR / RFID IDENTIFICATION
The Inventory Item Master shall support identification methods required across F&B and Retail.
Barcode
 Internal Barcode
 Supplier Barcode
 EAN
 UPC
 Code 128
QR
May be used for:
 Inventory Lookup
 Asset/Item Identification
 Mobile Operations
RFID
Where applicable:
 EPC
 RFID Tag Type
 Read Status
The matrix also requires barcode management at item-master level.
MULTI-TENANT & MULTI-COMPANY CONTROL
Inventory records must respect the TICVAI enterprise hierarchy.
An item may be:
Global to Tenant
or restricted to:
 Company
 Business Unit
 Park
 Venue
 Warehouse
 Module
Example:
Water Bottle
Global Item:
Yes
Used By:
Retail ✓
F&B ✓
Events ✓
This is important because TICVAI should not create separate "Retail Water Bottle" and "F&B Water Bottle" 
inventory records if they represent the same physical stock item.
SHARED ITEM VS MODULE PRODUCT
This distinction shall be explicit.
Inventory Item
Represents the physical stock-controlled object.

TICVAI / INVENTORY & PROCUREMENT BACKEND STRUCTURE
CONFIDENTIAL | 21
Examples:
Water Bottle
Beef Patty
T-Shirt Black/M
Cleaning Chemical
Retail Product
Represents something sold to the guest.
F&B Product
Represents a prepared menu item.
Procurement Item
References the same Inventory Item for purchasing.
Therefore:
One Inventory Item
may connect to:
Retail SKU
and/or
F&B Recipe
and/or
Procurement Supplier Catalog
without duplicate stock records.
APPROVAL ENGINE INTEGRATION
Board 1 shall use TICVAI's shared Approval Engine.
Examples:
New Inventory Item
→ Inventory Master Data Owner
Tracking Method Change
→ Inventory Manager
UOM Conversion Change
→ Inventory Manager / Finance where required
Negative Stock Override
→ Authorized Role
Reorder Policy Change
→ Inventory Manager
No separate approval mechanism shall be built solely for Inventory.
AUDIT REQUIREMENTS
The system shall maintain complete audit history for:
 Item Creation
 Item Modification
 Status Change
 Category Change
 UOM Change
 Barcode Change
 Batch Change
 Serial Change

TICVAI / INVENTORY & PROCUREMENT BACKEND STRUCTURE
