ARCHITECTURAL REQUIREMENT
This Board should establish one central TICVAI Inventory Ledger and Item Master.
SoftLab should not create separate inventory masters for:
Retail
F&B
Rental
Warehouse
Procurement
Instead:
Enterprise Inventory Item Master
↓
Stock Ledger
↓
Warehouse / Location / Bin
↓
Batch / Lot / Serial
↓
Quantity + Status
↓
Cost + Movement + Audit
Then operational modules consume the same inventory services.

TICVAI / INVENTORY & PROCUREMENT BACKEND STRUCTURE
CONFIDENTIAL | 24
That means, for example:
Retail sale
→ decrements the shared inventory ledger.
F&B burger sale
→ recipe consumption decrements the same shared inventory ledger.
Procurement receipt
→ increases the same shared inventory ledger.
Rental allocation
→ reserves inventory or an individual tracked item in the same platform-level architecture.
This Board becomes the foundation for every remaining Inventory & Procurement board, and it is the most 
important place to prevent duplicated stock data across TICVAI.

TICVAI / INVENTORY & PROCUREMENT BACKEND STRUCTURE
CONFIDENTIAL | 25
TICVAI INVENTORY & PROCUREMENT — BOARD 2
Warehouse, Location & Fulfilment Operations — Scope of Work
1. Purpose
The Warehouse, Location & Fulfilment Operations Board shall provide TICVAI with the centralized operational 
layer for managing warehouses, storage locations, zones, bins, receiving, put-away, internal warehouse 
movements, picking, packing, staging and dispatch.
Board 1 established what inventory exists and its enterprise stock position.
Board 2 shall establish:
Where is it physically located? How does it enter the warehouse? Where should it be stored? How is it → → →
picked? How is it packed? How does it leave? → →
The architecture shall follow:
Warehouse Zone Storage Location Bin Inventory Item Batch / Serial Stock Status Task → → → → → → → →
Movement Employee / Device Confirmation → →
Board 2 shall support warehouse operations serving:
 Food & Beverage
 Retail
 Rental
 Operations
 Maintenance
 Events
 Temporary / Event Warehouses
 Central Distribution Centers
 Venue Stores
 Back-of-House Storage

TICVAI / INVENTORY & PROCUREMENT BACKEND STRUCTURE
CONFIDENTIAL | 26
 Cold / Frozen Storage
 Secure Storage
 Quarantine Areas
It shall use the same Shared Inventory Ledger established in Board 1. Warehouse operations shall create 
controlled inventory movements against that ledger rather than maintaining a separate warehouse stock balance.
