OFFLINE / CONNECTIVITY HANDLING
Warehouse mobile workflows should support controlled offline behavior where required.
When connectivity is temporarily unavailable:
 Previously assigned tasks remain accessible where supported.
 Scans may be locally queued.
 Transactions should receive temporary device references.
 Synchronization occurs when connectivity returns.
 Conflicts shall be surfaced for resolution.
Example:
Item was moved by another user while device was offline.
TICVAI should not silently overwrite the newer inventory state.
