IMPORTANT ARCHITECTURAL BOUNDARY
There is one point I recommend we make very clear to SoftLab.
Board 2 is the Warehouse Execution layer.
It should not duplicate Board 1's Inventory Ledger, and it should not duplicate Procurement.
The architecture should be:
Board 1 — Inventory Master & Stock Ledger
provides:
Item + Quantity + Status + Batch + Serial + Cost + Movement
↓
Board 2 — Warehouse Execution
provides:
Warehouse + Zone + Bin + Receive + Put-Away + Pick + Pack + Stage + Dispatch
↓
Later:
Procurement Boards
provide:
Supplier + PR + RFQ + Quote + PO + Supplier Delivery
Therefore, when a warehouse employee moves 50 units from Receiving Dock 01 Bin A-04 → , Board 2 manages 
the physical workflow, but the transaction posts into the same Shared Inventory Ledger from Board 1.
This distinction will prevent SoftLab from accidentally building a separate Warehouse Management System with its
own inventory balance.
It also gives us the foundation for Board 3 — Transfers, Counts & Reconciliation, where we should handle 
enterprise transfers, physical/cycle counts, stock variance, adjustments and reconciliation across all locations.

TICVAI / INVENTORY & PROCUREMENT BACKEND STRUCTURE
CONFIDENTIAL | 51
TICVAI INVENTORY & PROCUREMENT — BOARD 3
Transfers, Stock Counts, Adjustments & Reconciliation — Scope of Work
1. Purpose
The Transfers, Stock Counts, Adjustments & Reconciliation Board shall provide TICVAI with the centralized control 
layer for moving inventory between locations, verifying physical stock, identifying discrepancies, approving 
adjustments, reconciling inventory balances, and maintaining complete stock accountability.
Board 1 established:
What inventory exists and how much stock TICVAI has.
Board 2 established:
Where inventory is physically stored and how warehouse operations execute receiving, put-away, picking, 
packing and dispatch.
Board 3 shall establish:
How stock moves between locations How physical stock is verified How discrepancies are investigated → →
→ → How corrections are controlled How the inventory ledger remains accurate.
The core architecture shall follow:
Transfer / Count Request Inventory Item Source Location Destination / Physical Quantity Variance → → → →
→ → → → → → Investigation Approval Adjustment Inventory Ledger Finance Impact Audit
Board 3 shall use the same Shared Inventory Ledger from Board 1 and the warehouse/location structure from 
Board 2.
