STOCK FREEZE & COUNT CONTROL
For physical counts, TICVAI should support configurable count policies.
Full Freeze
No inventory movements permitted during count.
Soft Freeze
Transactions continue but are separately tracked and reconciled.
Snapshot Count
System records inventory state at a specific timestamp.
Transactions after that timestamp do not alter the count baseline.
I strongly recommend supporting Snapshot Count, because many TICVAI customers—parks, attractions, 
restaurants and retail stores—cannot stop operations simply to perform inventory counting.
RECOUNT RULES
TICVAI should support automatic recount requirements.
Example:
First Count
System:
100
Physical:
92
Variance:
-8%
Configured Tolerance:
2%
Result:
Recount Required
The second counter may be different from the first where policy requires segregation of duties.
COUNT APPROVAL RULES
Example:
Variance AED 50 ≤
Inventory Supervisor
AED 50–1,000
Inventory Manager
AED 1,000–10,000
Operations / Finance
> AED 10,000
Senior Approval
These thresholds shall be tenant-configurable and use the common TICVAI Approval Engine.

