IMPORTANT ARCHITECTURAL REQUIREMENT
I recommend we make one boundary very clear to SoftLab:
Board 4 owns:
Supplier Master + Supplier Qualification + Supplier Catalog + Purchase Request + Internal Stock Check + 
Approval + Demand Consolidation
It should not yet own the complete RFQ, quotation and Purchase Order transaction lifecycle.
That belongs to the next board.
Therefore:
Board 4 — Procurement Initiation
Demand PR Approval Sourcing Requirement → → →
↓
Board 5 — Sourcing & Purchase Order
RFQ Supplier Quotes Comparison Negotiation Award PO → → → → →
↓
Later:
Receiving / GRN / Invoice Matching
This separation is important because otherwise Board 4 becomes overloaded and SoftLab may mix requesting 
something with commercially purchasing it.
The other architectural point I strongly recommend is the Internal Fulfilment Gate:
Before TICVAI purchases externally, it should always understand whether the requirement can be fulfilled 
from existing enterprise inventory.
That gives TICVAI a much stronger workflow than a conventional procurement system:
Need Check Transfer Procure only the remaining requirement. → → →
It connects the work we already completed across F&B, Retail, Shared Inventory, Warehouse and Inventory 
Control into one coherent procurement architecture.

