ARCHITECTURAL REQUIREMENT
Board 5 should own the commercial sourcing and Purchase Order lifecycle, but it should not duplicate supplier 
onboarding from Board 4 or warehouse receiving from Board 2.
The correct architecture is:
Board 4 — Procurement Initiation
Supplier + PR + Internal Stock Check + Approval + Demand Consolidation
↓
Board 5 — Sourcing & Commercial Commitment
RFQ + Quotation + Evaluation + Negotiation + Award + Purchase Order
↓
Board 6 — Procurement Receiving & Financial Matching
Supplier Delivery + Receipt + GRN + Inspection + Invoice + Three-Way Match + Discrepancy + Closure
The most important principle for this Board is:
TICVAI should recommend the best procurement decision based on total business value—not automatically
choose the cheapest quotation.
Price matters, but so do:
Delivery Quality Compliance MOQ Reliability Required Date Total Cost Operational Risk. → → → → → → →
This is particularly important because procurement is directly connected to the rest of TICVAI: a cheaper supplier 
that delivers after an event, after a restaurant stock-out, or after a high-demand retail period can ultimately cost 
the customer far more than the difference in unit price.

TICVAI / INVENTORY & PROCUREMENT BACKEND STRUCTURE
CONFIDENTIAL | 124
TICVAI INVENTORY & PROCUREMENT — BOARD 6
Receiving, GRN, Invoice Matching & Procurement Closure — Scope of Work
1. Purpose
The Receiving, GRN, Invoice Matching & Procurement Closure Board shall provide TICVAI with the centralized 
control layer for completing the procurement lifecycle after a Purchase Order has been issued.
Board 5 established:
RFQ Supplier Quotation Evaluation Award Purchase Order Supplier Acknowledgement → → → → →
Board 6 shall establish:
What did the supplier actually deliver? Was the correct quantity and quality received? What inventory → →
should become available? Does the supplier invoice match the PO and receipt? Are discrepancies within → →
tolerance? Can the transaction be financially cleared and the PO closed? →
The core architecture shall follow:
Purchase Order Supplier Delivery Receiving Inspection GRN Inventory Update Supplier Invoice → → → → → →
→ → → → 2-Way / 3-Way Match Exception Resolution Finance PO Closure
This Board shall integrate directly with:
Procurement + Warehouse + Shared Inventory + Finance + Supplier Management + Approval Engine + 
Employee App + AI
A key architectural principle is that Board 6 must not duplicate the physical warehouse functionality already 
designed in Board 2. Board 2 executes the physical receiving and put-away operation; Board 6 controls the 
procurement receipt, GRN, matching, financial handoff and PO closure.

